<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clement Attlee</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1883–1967</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clement Attlee was a British Labour politician and prime minister of the United Kingdom from 1945 to 1951. Deputy prime minister in Churchill's wartime coalition, he led Labour to a landslide victory in 1945; his government nationalised major industries, created the National Health Service and the welfare state, and granted independence to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clement-attlee.jpg" alt="Clement Attlee" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Presumably Yousuf Karsh · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Person_attlee2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
